# Participant data. Nothing under here may ever reach the remote: the raw
# college records, the nursing workbooks and the SID-to-index linkage table
# are all directly or indirectly identifying.
data/
*.xlsx
*.xls
anonymised_records.csv
raw_college_records.*
*linkage*
*_linkage.csv

# The HMAC key that pseudonymises index numbers. Publishing it would make
# every pseudonym in every released table reversible by dictionary attack.
/local

# Ethics paperwork, consent forms, questionnaires, and the reference thesis
# collection. Third-party work and signed documents.
/proposal

# Generated artefacts. Every one is reproducible from the notebooks.
/results
*.pkl
*.docx

# Environments
ml_env/
venv/
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tooling
.gstack/

# The test suite. Held locally rather than published: it reads docs/manuscript/
# and results/, neither of which is in this repository, so a clone could not run
# it. What it verifies is described in README.md and in the covering note.
tests/

# Corpus construction and writing tools. The consolidation scripts parse the
# specific institutional workbook layouts and do nothing without data/, which is
# restricted; the rest convert manuscript drafts between formats.
scripts/

# The written thesis. The manuscript, the literature review and the earlier
# submissions are kept local rather than published alongside the code that
# reproduces them. Nothing under here is needed to run the pipeline, but the
# manuscript-consistency tests read docs/manuscript/, so those tests cannot run
# from a clone of this repository alone.
docs/

# The *linkage* rule above keeps the SID-to-index table out of git. It also
# catches this analysis script by name. The script contains code, not data.
!notebooks/06_linkage_attack.py

# Agent working notes. Local only, never published.
/AGENT.md
/HANDOFF_PROMPT.md

# The working queue. Local only: it tracks thesis progress rather than the method.
/TODO.md
